     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-19 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>1 Finance Secures SEBI Approval for Passive Funds</h1>
       
       <p>1 Finance has received in-principle approval from SEBI for an MF Lite licence, signaling its entry into the mutual fund sector. The company plans to launch passive mutual funds during Q4 FY27.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/1-finance-secures-sebi-approval-for-passive-funds.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>For ordinary savers and taxpayers, this development is significant because SEBI's MF Lite framework aims to ease regulatory requirements for eligible passive fund houses. This regulatory change could encourage new players to enter the market.</p><p>The introduction of new entities like 1 Finance is expected to foster greater competition among fund providers. Ultimately, this could expand investor choice, particularly within index funds and Exchange Traded Funds (ETFs), offering more options for passive investing.</p><p>What to watch: New passive mutual fund options are expected to emerge in Q4 FY27.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately covers all available details from the brief source material without padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
