     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-19 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by News18 India, India Today">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Delhi Court Extends Judicial Custody of CJP Leaders Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A Delhi court has extended the judicial custody of Cockroach Janta Party leaders Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka until October 21. The two activists were originally arrested on October 14 and lodged in Tihar Jail for allegedly violating peace bonds and trespassing at Jantar Mantar. They had breached barricades and entered the area without authorization while demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. Police registered a case against them for trespassing, violating prohibitory orders, breaching peace bonds, and obstructing public servants. The arrests occurred amid heightened security following protests against electoral roll revisions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/delhi-court-extends-judicial-custody-of-cjp-leaders-saurav-d.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Directly reports the custody extension, dates, charges, and background without straying from the source facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source · also covered by 1 more</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/judicial-custody-of-cjps-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka-extended-by-two-days-10389189.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/judicial-custody-of-cjps-ashutosh-ranka-saurav-das-extended-for-two-days-by-special-executive-magistrate-3020902-2026-10-19?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>This brief was written from the original report. The same event was independently covered by the other outlets listed here.</p>
    </div>
