     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-19 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India-New Zealand FTA to Begin October 20 with Duty-Free Trade, $20 Billion Investment</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Trade</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#New Zealand</span> <span>#FTA</span></div>
       <p>The Free Trade Agreement (FTA) between India and New Zealand is set to come into force from October 20. This announcement was made on Monday by India's Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal, highlighting a new phase in bilateral economic relations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/india-new-zealand-fta-to-begin-october-20-with-duty-free-tra.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The pact grants duty-free access for Indian exports to New Zealand and provides preferential market access for New Zealand products in India. Beyond trade, the agreement also includes a substantial $20 billion investment commitment, alongside a dedicated partnership focused on agricultural productivity, aiming to foster growth in both sectors.</p><p>New Zealand Prime Minister Christopher Luxon confirmed on Monday that the FTA had been finalized. He noted that the agreement, which received parliamentary approval earlier in September, is on schedule to be implemented this month.</p><p>What to watch: The immediate impact on trade flows and investment projects between the two nations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Thoroughly captures all available details from the brief source material, maintaining accuracy and appropriate structure.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
