       <h1>Laal Hit Janta Party Emerges to Counter CJP Protests</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A new group, the Laal Hit Janta Party, has emerged in New Delhi as a satirical counter to the Cockroach Janata Party (CJP), which is currently protesting for the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. Led by Ayan Bhatnagar, the group advocates for constitutional adherence and peaceful democratic participation, explicitly opposing the CJP's methods.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/laal-hit-janta-party-emerges-to-counter-cjp-protests.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The organization, which held a recent meeting at Malviya Smriti Bhawan, focuses on promoting factual debate over alleged electoral irregularities. While the CJP and various student groups continue to protest over disputed voter roll revisions, the Laal Hit Janta Party maintains it will not contest elections, instead choosing to challenge the CJP's presence through public discourse.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the emergence of the Laal Hit Janta Party as a satirical counter-movement, including key details on their goals and activities.</p>
