     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-19 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mandhana's India Clinch T20I Series Against Zimbabwe with Dominant Nine-Wicket Win</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India Women</span> <span>#T20I</span> <span>#Smriti Mandhana</span></div>
       <p>Smriti Mandhana commenced her tenure as India's full-time T20I captain with a commanding series victory, as India defeated Zimbabwe by nine wickets in the second T20I. This win sealed the series with one match remaining, after India successfully chased a target of 103 runs in just 8.5 overs, finishing on 104/1. The contest was thoroughly one-sided, with India securing the win with 67 balls to spare, marking the most balls remaining in a 100-plus chase in women's T20Is.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/mandhanas-india-clinch-t20i-series-against-zimbabwe-with-dom.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Shafali Verma spearheaded India's batting charge, smashing a 24-ball half-century that included six fours and four sixes, ending her innings on 55. Captain Mandhana remained unbeaten on 47, sealing the victory with a six. The opening duo of Verma and Mandhana recorded India's second-best Powerplay score in women's T20Is, racing to 76/0 within the first six overs. Shafali's score of 55 was her ninth fifty-plus score in 2026, the most by any player in a calendar year in women's T20Is. Their partnership also marked the ninth 50-plus opening stand between them in 2026, a joint-record for a calendar year in women's T20I cricket.</p><p>Earlier, India's bowlers kept Zimbabwe under tight control throughout their innings, restricting them to 102/8. Nandani Sharma clean-bowled Zimbabwe opener Kelis Ndhlovu in the fourth over, with the hosts crawling to 20/1 at the end of the Powerplay. Niki Prasad then made a significant impact, striking twice in the first two balls of her spell to finish with figures of 2/7, becoming only the third player in men's and women's T20I history to achieve this feat. Although Chipo Mugeri-Tiripano top-scored with 34 and shared a 45-run stand with captain Josephine Nkomo, Zimbabwe's innings never gained significant momentum.</p><p>What to watch: The final T20I offers India a chance for a clean sweep under new captain Smriti Mandhana.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reports the match details, player records, and contextual statistics provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/smriti-mandhana-wins-first-series-as-india-captain-after-nine-wicket-rout-of-zimbabwe-in-2nd-t20i/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
