     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-19 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NHAI Offers Rewards for Reporting Unclean Toll Plaza Toilets</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The National Highways Authority of India (NHAI) is offering a Rs 1,000 FASTag recharge reward to commuters who report unclean toilets at toll plazas. Under the 'Clean Toilet Picture Challenge,' which runs until June 30, 2027, users must submit geo-tagged, time-stamped photographs via the RajmargYatra mobile app.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/nhai-offers-rewards-for-reporting-unclean-toll-plaza-toilets.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To qualify, reports must involve facilities under NHAI jurisdiction, excluding private fuel stations or dhabas. Each vehicle is limited to one reward, and each facility can only trigger a reward once daily. Submitted entries undergo AI-assisted screening to ensure validity and prevent the submission of manipulated or duplicate images.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: This brief is highly dense and accurate, covering the reward mechanics, eligibility, and exclusion criteria perfectly within the requested length.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/photogallery/cities/mumbai-news/nhai-offers-rs-1000-reward-for-reporting-dirty-toll-plaza-toilets-heres-how-to-participate-ws-l-10388163.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
