     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-19 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>PFRDA Launches NPS Central for Streamlined Pension Management</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Personal Finance</span> <span>#Pensions</span> <span>#NPS</span> <span>#Digital Platform</span></div>
       <p>The Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA) has launched NPS Central, a new digital platform designed to offer National Pension System (NPS) subscribers a unified portal for enrolment, investment, and account management. The platform, launched on NPS Diwas, October 1, 2026, was jointly developed and is managed by the three Central Recordkeeping Agencies (CRAs) under NPS: Protean, KFintech, and CAMS. This initiative aims to enhance subscriber convenience, transparency, and ease of investment, fostering a more integrated pension ecosystem.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/pfrda-launches-nps-central-for-streamlined-pension-managemen.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Existing NPS subscribers can now log in using only their registered mobile number and date of birth, authenticated via a one-time password (OTP), eliminating the need to recall their Permanent Retirement Account Number (PRAN). Upon logging in, subscribers are presented with a single dashboard that provides a comprehensive view of their NPS accounts and investment portfolios across all three CRAs. The platform, accessible at www.npscentral.in, allows users to contribute to existing schemes, explore and opt for new ones, compare scheme features, returns, and charges, and update their profile details.</p><p>Further functionalities for existing subscribers include downloading account statements and tracking the status of contributions made through various modes. The platform also integrates the Pension Sahayak portal, enabling subscribers to raise grievances or seek clarity on services. For new subscribers, NPS Central offers AI-assisted onboarding, with Central KYC (CKYC) and DigiLocker available as KYC options, complemented by an AI-enabled assistant to answer queries. New applicants can explore and compare investment schemes, review their performance, and select a pension fund, receiving an electronic PRAN (e-PRAN) and essential account services upon successful registration, with onboarding charges typically set at nil.</p><p>NPS Central also facilitates registration for NPS Swasthya, which combines a dedicated investment corpus with a super top-up health insurance arrangement. PFRDA plans to expand the platform in phases, introducing features such as options to change investment choices and pension funds, apply for loans against NPS, set up systematic investment plan (SIP) mandates, and manage NPS Vatsalya accounts. Future enhancements will also include corporate onboarding, re-KYC, and NPS Tier II account-related facilities, with API specifications made available for ecosystem integration.</p><p>What to watch: Future phases will introduce loans, SIP mandates, and corporate onboarding.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Excellent reporting that thoroughly details the launch, features, login methods, and future roadmap of NPS Central.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/pfrda-launches-nps-central-how-simplified-pension-portal-works-who-can-use-how-to-log-in-top-features-explained-11792412779893.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
