     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-10-19 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rare Disease Patients Seek PM's Aid for Treatment Funds</h1>
       
       <p>LSDSS has reported that patients suffering from progressive, potentially life-threatening rare diseases are currently facing interruptions in their ongoing treatment regimens.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/rare-disease-patients-seek-pms-aid-for-treatment-funds.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>These critical treatment interruptions are occurring because the patients have fully exhausted their previously sanctioned financial assistance, leaving them without the necessary funds to continue their care.</p><p>In response to this urgent situation, the LSDSS stated that these patients are now seeking the Prime Minister’s intervention to secure additional financial assistance to ensure their continued access to vital treatment.</p><p>What to watch: The Prime Minister's office for a response to the funding request.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Clean wire brief that accurately reflects the source statement without unnecessary fluff.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/rare-disease-patients-seek-pms-intervention-to-secure-additional-funds-for-treatment/135047625" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
