     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-19 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Report: 82% Indian Students Concerned AI Hinders Deep Learning</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Students</span> <span>#Report</span></div>
       <p>A recent report highlights a significant concern among Indian students regarding the impact of Artificial Intelligence (AI) on their education. According to the findings, a large majority of students express apprehension about AI's role in accelerating academic tasks.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-19/report-82-indian-students-concerned-ai-hinders-deep-learning.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Specifically, 82% of Indian students fear that while AI may speed up work processes, it does so at the cost of fostering deep learning. This sentiment suggests a potential challenge in integrating AI tools into educational frameworks while preserving comprehensive understanding.</p><p>What to watch: Further studies on AI's impact on educational outcomes and learning methodologies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the provided source snippet.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
